@startuml get_user

' Participantes conforme classe/simples/user.puml: sem mapper e sem a interface JPA.
' O filtro de status DELETED mora no UserRepositoryImpl, não no caso de uso: é ele que
' escolhe a variante ...AndStatusNot do repositório JPA.

title GET /users e GET /users/{id}: Buscar Usuário

actor "Administrador" as Ator
boundary "Frontend" as FE
participant "UserController" as Ctrl
participant "GetUserUseCase" as UC
participant "UserRepositoryPort" as Port
participant "UserRepositoryImpl" as Impl
database "users" as DB

== Listar todos ==

Ator -> FE: abre a lista de usuários
activate FE
FE -> Ctrl: GET /users
activate Ctrl

Ctrl -> UC: findAll()
activate UC

UC -> Port: findAll()
activate Port
Port -> Impl: findAll()
activate Impl
Impl -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE status<>'DELETED'
DB --> Impl: List<User>
Impl --> Port: List<User>
deactivate Impl
Port --> UC: List<User>
deactivate Port

UC --> Ctrl: List<UserResponse>
deactivate UC
Ctrl --> FE: 200 OK [UserResponse]
deactivate Ctrl
FE --> Ator: exibe a lista
deactivate FE

== Buscar por id ==

Ator -> FE: abre um usuário
activate FE
FE -> Ctrl: GET /users/{id}
activate Ctrl

Ctrl -> UC: findById(id)
activate UC

UC -> Port: findById(UserId.of(id))
activate Port
Port -> Impl: findById(userId)
activate Impl
Impl -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE id=? AND status<>'DELETED'
DB --> Impl: Optional<User>
Impl --> Port: Optional<User>
deactivate Impl
Port --> UC: Optional<User>
deactivate Port

alt usuário encontrado
  UC --> Ctrl: UserResponse
  Ctrl --> FE: 200 OK {UserResponse}
  FE --> Ator: exibe os dados
else não encontrado, ou já deletado
  UC --> Ctrl: ResourceNotFoundException
  Ctrl --> FE: 404 Not Found\nNOT_FOUND
  FE --> Ator: exibe erro
end

deactivate UC
deactivate Ctrl
deactivate FE

@enduml
